sequenceDiagram
    participant UI as Hold screen
    participant C as BookingController
    participant S as BookingService
    participant J as ReleaseJob
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    loop UI-07 open, including restoration after reload
        UI->>C: heartbeat(holdId) every 10 seconds
        C->>S: heartbeat(userId, holdId)
        S-->>UI: current status, fixed expiresAt, fresh serverNow
    end
    alt known presence missing for 30 seconds
        J->>S: releaseAbandonedHolds(now)
        S->>DB: lock ACTIVE hold, recheck absence and release all its rows
        DB-->>S: RELEASED; otherwise release pending and retry
    else fixed expiry reached (also fallback after process restart)
        J->>S: releaseExpiredHolds(now)
        S->>DB: mark EXPIRED, release schedule rows atomically
        DB-->>S: RELEASED; otherwise retain EXPIRED and retry
    end
    UI->>C: getActiveHold(holdId) or releaseHold(holdId)
    C->>S: getActiveHold(userId, holdId) or releaseHold(userId, holdId)
    S-->>UI: Releasing / ReleaseFailed / Released
    Note over UI,DB: Reload preserves the same hold and expiry; unknown presence falls back to expiry. Return to selection only after release.
